 "range_method": "Per anatomical angle (lib.environment.actors.motion.anatomy, each skeleton in its own calibrated frame), the cited clinical range intersected with the natural envelope widened by 5 degrees. The envelope is the raw capture's p0.1-p99.9 over both sides (59,154 frames; the p0.5-p99.5 band cut the real lunges: hip flexion p99.5 47 degrees against recorded lunges to 95), except where the suit's estimate does not describe the rig ('envelope_source'): the rigs' own authored clips, or the clinical range alone. The shoulder's plane of elevation is bounded only above 45 degrees of elevation. 'gated' marks the angles the motion gates hold (the arm, clavicle and spine, which the arm IK controls); the rest are reported.",
 "gate_method": "The motion gates' joint-limit check uses 'gate_range_deg', not 'range_deg' (the arm IK's target). Per side: where the clinical range binds, the clinical bound (hard); where the natural envelope binds, the furthest the envelope's source went ('natural_extremes_deg': the capture's or the rigs' clips' minimum and maximum), capped by the clinical bound. Joints-v1's gate counted every frame outside the p0.1-p99.9 band plus 5 degrees, a percentile membership that a union over every gated angle on both sides fails on natural frames by construction (datagen-bodies' donor build, 2026-10-07: 15.7% of conditioned capture frames); excursions are now judged by magnitude against the natural extremes.",
 "hinge_azimuth_deg": {
